BC-to-PPO handoff independent verification, round 1

HEAD 5349e96d10db2582973b2b3878f2d3b0a980934c; BASE 218a05b8b00d945f04317aeedbc3c1972c62aaff. Integration configs archived read-only at 5b43062fdab6c63d20d3f92f1e51b93b1b025b2c. All work CPU-only, OMP_NUM_THREADS=2. No production training/GPU work or tracked modifications.

Findings:

1. P2, scripts/run_ppo.py:1085–1089: the teacher_init/initial-last-best loader accepts top-level opponent_id and hidden_state alongside valid model weights. This is pre-existing and disclosed, but the explicitly adopted checkpoint schema rule requires rejection, not merely ignoring fields. Both actual PPOTrainer loaders reject them. Fix by sharing an allowed-top-level-key validator that does not require optimizer/PPO metadata, preserving minimal {'model': ...} checkpoints and LoRA base loading, then cover the two offending fields with a focused loader test. Evidence: /tmp/kg-bc-handoff-r1-semantics/schema_probe.py and schema_probe.txt.
2. P3, cookbook/references/bc-best-starts-ppo-with-a-fresh-critic-head.md:23 (also README.md:495, ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/bc-handoff/README.md:43, note metadata/index/log): 97.2% is 700/720 seat-value predictions, not turn rows. Both seats saturate on 345/360 turns; either on 355/360. From turn 20 the cell rate is 693/700 = 99%. The gradient probe compares each model against its own opposite-sign prediction, not one common flipped game outcome. The all-wins selection and saturation support selection bias, but do not establish learned team-identity detection. Correct the denominator/scope and label identity attribution as a hypothesis. At Reference line 25 clarify Isaiah had no BC-to-PPO path, not no critic.

Verified semantics:

- Saved BC config and eager/2-/4-/8-rank launch configs have equal model, observation and action sections; CPU forwards disable only force_flash_attn.
